ng, string, number]. The numbers are floats from the input distances? They could be floats. We keep them as floats. total_weight is float sum.\n\nEdge case: The input may not be sorted; we sort. All good.\n\nNow produce the JSON object: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n        if u < v:\\n            edges.append((mr, u, v))\\n        else:\\n            edges.append((mr, v, u))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is disconnected; cannot form MST.')\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"}\n\nBut that's not JSON because newlines are literal. We need to escape them. So we create a single-line string with \\n sequences. I'll manually replace each newline with \\n. However, the code has indentation using spaces; we preserve spaces. The newline and indentation must be represented.\n\nI'll write the escaped string. Let me do it ste